<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Leong Finance 1996 net up 14.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Hong Leong Finance 1996 net up 14.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     87.39 vs  76.14</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    9.0  vs   9.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    38.81 vs  33.82</p>
<p>Group shr fully diluted (cents)  32.81 vs  29.28</p>
<p>    Operating income		    373.96 vs 352.00</p>
<p>    Investment income		     9.70 vs   9.50</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   15.61 vs  16.20</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		3.26 vs   2.94</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			135.42 vs 124.23</p>
<p>    Tax					37.17 vs  41.01</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (loss) 10.86 vs   7.08  (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Hong Leong Finance Ltd is a finance company. It said profit for the year had been arrived at after making additional general provisions for doubtful debts amounting to S$10.4 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
